      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just wanted to note, i looked into this a bit more to see whether this is an actual bug that can be trigerred, and not just a hypothetical one, and I think it is. \n\nA VMM can choose any vCPU as the primary (0 is by convention, nothing that enforces it). A misbehaving VMM could call KVM_RUN on vCPU 1 (populating vm-\u003evcpus[1]) but skip 0. vCPU 1 could then issue the SMC to set up FFA or IOMMU. Later, it performs a teardown, which triggers this.\n\nI am happy to explore ways to fix this. A refactor to use VM is the best approach, if you think the churn is ok. In that case, better to have it as its own series. What do you think?",
      "revId": "2a0eb5ebfef4322e503ccaf7845b9ee564a41848",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
